[7] THE PRE-REGISTERED READING

  reading: IMAGE-BORNE
  the image cell (3) converts and the proprio cell (4) does not: the park's win is the sightline; a recollection's own A/B is the shipping path

  The between-cell contrast is the design-valid leg (the cells diverge after
  the first call, so no per-episode pairing is used). Cells 3/4 are OOD input
  pairs: a positive names the channel and does not ship; a null is weak
  evidence (PREREG section 8). The asymmetry is measured
  (logs/p36/ood_proprio.txt): cell 3 writes the in-support ready proprio
  (max |z| = 0.59 of the 7 channels, direct store; 0.37 of the training
  store) under the parked image; cell 4 writes the parked proprio under the
  shipped image, and that vector's j2 (-0.978 rad) sits at -4.26 sigma of
  the direct store and -5.13 of the training store, 3 of the 7 channels
  beyond 1.7 sigma. So a cell-4 positive is the stronger read (the park's
  own proprio, alone, on an in-support image) and a cell-4 null the weaker
  one (a 4-sigma input may simply be ignored or unrepresented).
